1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,591
One computer cannot build everything.

2
00:00:03,141 --> 00:00:04,648
A team has Linux builds,

3
00:00:04,648 --> 00:00:05,590
Windows builds,

4
00:00:05,590 --> 00:00:06,281
slow tests,

5
00:00:06,281 --> 00:00:08,480
and ten developers pushing at once.

6
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:10,553
If one machine does all the work,

7
00:00:10,553 --> 00:00:12,186
everybody waits in a line.

8
00:00:12,736 --> 00:00:14,809
Jenkins solves this with agents.

9
00:00:14,809 --> 00:00:16,752
The controller plans the work.

10
00:00:16,752 --> 00:00:17,594
Agents do it,

11
00:00:17,594 --> 00:00:18,760
on other machines,

12
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:19,861
at the same time.

13
00:00:20,411 --> 00:00:22,070
Today you add a real agent,

14
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:23,544
send a real build to it,

15
00:00:23,544 --> 00:00:26,001
and learn where the files go afterwards.

16
00:00:27,551 --> 00:00:28,980
Here is what to expect.

17
00:00:29,530 --> 00:00:33,050
One: the words. Controller, agent, executor, label.

18
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,462
Two: where the files live. Workspace, artifacts, and the stash.

19
00:00:38,012 --> 00:00:39,283
Three: a live demo,

20
00:00:39,283 --> 00:00:41,158
in the real Jenkins screens.

21
00:00:41,158 --> 00:00:42,228
We add an agent,

22
00:00:42,228 --> 00:00:43,433
send builds to it,

23
00:00:43,433 --> 00:00:45,709
watch two builds run side by side,

24
00:00:45,709 --> 00:00:46,512
keep a file,

25
00:00:46,512 --> 00:00:48,721
and pass a file between machines.

26
00:00:49,271 --> 00:00:52,087
Four: the common mistakes, and where to find the lab.

27
00:00:52,637 --> 00:00:55,602
This is objective seven of the Jenkins domain.

28
00:00:57,652 --> 00:00:58,868
Four words to know.

29
00:00:59,418 --> 00:01:01,864
The controller is the brain of Jenkins.

30
00:01:01,864 --> 00:01:02,993
It keeps the jobs,

31
00:01:02,993 --> 00:01:03,746
the history,

32
00:01:03,746 --> 00:01:04,812
and the settings.

33
00:01:04,812 --> 00:01:06,129
It decides what runs,

34
00:01:06,129 --> 00:01:06,757
and where.

35
00:01:07,307 --> 00:01:08,960
An agent is another machine,

36
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:09,904
or another user,

37
00:01:09,904 --> 00:01:11,262
that does the building.

38
00:01:11,262 --> 00:01:13,033
It connects to the controller,

39
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:14,155
and waits for work.

40
00:01:14,705 --> 00:01:17,440
An executor is one build slot on a machine.

41
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:21,510
An agent with two executors can run two builds at the same time.

42
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:24,060
A label is a tag on a machine.

43
00:01:24,060 --> 00:01:25,927
A pipeline asks for a label,

44
00:01:25,927 --> 00:01:27,127
for example maven,

45
00:01:27,127 --> 00:01:30,060
and Jenkins picks any machine that wears it.

46
00:01:30,610 --> 00:01:34,173
So the pipeline never names a machine. It names what it needs.

47
00:01:35,723 --> 00:01:37,430
Now, where do the files live?

48
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,647
Every job gets a workspace.

49
00:01:39,647 --> 00:01:40,574
It is a folder,

50
00:01:40,574 --> 00:01:42,550
on the agent that ran the build.

51
00:01:42,550 --> 00:01:44,403
The code is checked out there,

52
00:01:44,403 --> 00:01:46,812
and the build writes its results there.

53
00:01:47,362 --> 00:01:52,610
A workspace is working space, not storage. It can be wiped, and it stays on one machine.

54
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,232
To keep a result,

55
00:01:54,232 --> 00:01:54,925
archive it.

56
00:01:54,925 --> 00:01:59,023
The archiveArtifacts step copies chosen files to the controller,

57
00:01:59,023 --> 00:02:00,474
attached to that build,

58
00:02:00,474 --> 00:02:01,672
for download later.

59
00:02:02,222 --> 00:02:04,257
To pass a file to a later stage,

60
00:02:04,257 --> 00:02:06,102
maybe on a different machine,

61
00:02:06,102 --> 00:02:07,565
use stash and unstash.

62
00:02:07,565 --> 00:02:10,682
Stash saves files for the rest of this one build.

63
00:02:10,682 --> 00:02:12,209
Un stash puts them back,

64
00:02:12,209 --> 00:02:12,782
anywhere.

65
00:02:13,332 --> 00:02:18,452
Archive is for people, and for history. Stash is for the pipeline, for the next stage.

66
00:02:20,002 --> 00:02:21,054
A real Jenkins.

67
00:02:21,054 --> 00:02:22,386
I sign in as admin.

68
00:02:22,386 --> 00:02:25,682
On the left is the Build Executor Status panel.

69
00:02:25,682 --> 00:02:27,155
There is one machine,

70
00:02:27,155 --> 00:02:28,417
the built in node,

71
00:02:28,417 --> 00:02:30,591
and its two executors are idle.

72
00:02:30,591 --> 00:02:32,695
That is the controller itself.

73
00:02:33,245 --> 00:02:34,648
Now we add an agent.

74
00:02:34,648 --> 00:02:35,700
Manage Jenkins,

75
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,471
then Nodes.

76
00:02:36,471 --> 00:02:37,663
Here is the list.

77
00:02:37,663 --> 00:02:39,276
Only the built in node,

78
00:02:39,276 --> 00:02:39,837
for now.

79
00:02:40,387 --> 00:02:40,997
New Node.

80
00:02:40,997 --> 00:02:41,675
I name it,

81
00:02:41,675 --> 00:02:42,759
build agent one.

82
00:02:42,759 --> 00:02:44,656
The type is Permanent Agent,

83
00:02:44,656 --> 00:02:46,078
a machine that stays.

84
00:02:46,078 --> 00:02:46,553
Create.

85
00:02:52,103 --> 00:02:53,198
Now its settings.

86
00:02:53,198 --> 00:02:56,998
The remote root directory is the folder where it will work,

87
00:02:56,998 --> 00:02:58,865
the workspaces live under it.

88
00:02:58,865 --> 00:02:59,832
The labels are,

89
00:02:59,832 --> 00:03:00,218
linux,

90
00:03:00,218 --> 00:03:00,862
and maven.

91
00:03:00,862 --> 00:03:02,408
The number of executors,

92
00:03:02,408 --> 00:03:03,245
I set to two.

93
00:03:03,245 --> 00:03:09,300
The launch method is already the one we want: launch agent by connecting it to the controller.

94
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:10,523
The agent calls us,

95
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:12,005
so no firewall problem.

96
00:03:12,005 --> 00:03:12,327
Save.

97
00:03:24,877 --> 00:03:26,233
The new node appears,

98
00:03:26,233 --> 00:03:27,332
with a red cross.

99
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:28,818
Jenkins knows about it,

100
00:03:28,818 --> 00:03:30,950
but no machine has connected yet.

101
00:03:30,950 --> 00:03:31,467
Open it,

102
00:03:31,467 --> 00:03:35,666
and Jenkins prints the exact command to run on the other machine,

103
00:03:35,666 --> 00:03:36,571
with a secret,

104
00:03:36,571 --> 00:03:38,251
and the WebSocket option,

105
00:03:38,251 --> 00:03:40,706
so the agent uses the normal web port.

106
00:03:49,256 --> 00:03:50,654
On the other machine,

107
00:03:50,654 --> 00:03:52,184
I run that one command.

108
00:03:52,184 --> 00:03:55,978
Here the other machine is a second user on this computer,

109
00:03:55,978 --> 00:03:56,843
called agent.

110
00:03:56,843 --> 00:03:59,106
It is java dash jar agent dot jar,

111
00:03:59,106 --> 00:03:59,904
the address,

112
00:03:59,904 --> 00:04:00,503
the name,

113
00:04:00,503 --> 00:04:01,501
and the secret.

114
00:04:12,051 --> 00:04:13,476
Back to the node list.

115
00:04:13,476 --> 00:04:14,901
The red cross is gone.

116
00:04:14,901 --> 00:04:16,585
Build agent one is online,

117
00:04:16,585 --> 00:04:17,816
with two executors,

118
00:04:17,816 --> 00:04:21,054
and it shows its own disk space and response time.

119
00:04:21,604 --> 00:04:22,992
Now the simplest use.

120
00:04:22,992 --> 00:04:23,984
A new Pipeline,

121
00:04:23,984 --> 00:04:25,108
named agent test.

122
00:04:25,108 --> 00:04:27,488
The script asks for the label maven.

123
00:04:27,488 --> 00:04:29,273
It prints the machine name,

124
00:04:29,273 --> 00:04:29,868
the user,

125
00:04:29,868 --> 00:04:30,860
and the folder,

126
00:04:30,860 --> 00:04:32,579
then waits twenty seconds.

127
00:04:32,579 --> 00:04:34,959
I will explain the wait in a moment.

128
00:04:42,509 --> 00:04:42,871
Save,

129
00:04:42,871 --> 00:04:43,885
and Build Now.

130
00:04:43,885 --> 00:04:45,116
Open the console.

131
00:04:45,116 --> 00:04:48,592
The first lines say: running on build agent one,

132
00:04:48,592 --> 00:04:50,475
in slash home slash agent,

133
00:04:50,475 --> 00:04:51,489
slash Jenkins,

134
00:04:51,489 --> 00:04:52,648
slash workspace,

135
00:04:52,648 --> 00:04:53,879
slash agent test.

136
00:04:54,429 --> 00:04:55,904
That is the workspace.

137
00:04:55,904 --> 00:04:57,178
It is on the agent,

138
00:04:57,178 --> 00:04:59,121
under the agent's own folder,

139
00:04:59,121 --> 00:05:00,596
not on the controller.

140
00:05:00,596 --> 00:05:01,803
The user is agent,

141
00:05:01,803 --> 00:05:02,607
not Jenkins.

142
00:05:02,607 --> 00:05:03,813
Different machine,

143
00:05:03,813 --> 00:05:04,819
different user,

144
00:05:04,819 --> 00:05:05,757
same pipeline.

145
00:05:06,307 --> 00:05:11,363
Now executors. Build Now, three times, quickly. That is the reason for the wait.

146
00:05:11,913 --> 00:05:13,671
Look at the executor panel.

147
00:05:13,671 --> 00:05:15,754
Build agent one runs two builds,

148
00:05:15,754 --> 00:05:17,121
one on each executor.

149
00:05:17,121 --> 00:05:19,400
The third build waits in the queue,

150
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:20,767
until a slot is free.

151
00:05:21,317 --> 00:05:23,786
A queue means you need more executors,

152
00:05:23,786 --> 00:05:24,760
or more agents.

153
00:05:24,760 --> 00:05:26,449
Jenkins shows the problem,

154
00:05:26,449 --> 00:05:27,034
honestly.

155
00:05:27,584 --> 00:05:28,277
Now files.

156
00:05:28,277 --> 00:05:29,316
A new Pipeline,

157
00:05:29,316 --> 00:05:30,909
named cloud cart agent.

158
00:05:30,909 --> 00:05:33,887
This script builds cloud cart on the agent,

159
00:05:33,887 --> 00:05:34,649
with Maven.

160
00:05:34,649 --> 00:05:36,934
Then it archives the web archive,

161
00:05:36,934 --> 00:05:37,973
and stashes it.

162
00:05:45,523 --> 00:05:48,459
The second stage asks for a different machine,

163
00:05:48,459 --> 00:05:49,608
the built in node.

164
00:05:49,608 --> 00:05:51,076
It unstashes the file,

165
00:05:51,076 --> 00:05:51,905
and lists it.

166
00:05:51,905 --> 00:05:52,225
Save,

167
00:05:52,225 --> 00:05:53,118
and Build Now.

168
00:05:53,668 --> 00:05:54,878
Open the console.

169
00:05:54,878 --> 00:05:57,584
Stage one: running on build agent one.

170
00:05:57,584 --> 00:05:59,364
Maven builds the package,

171
00:05:59,364 --> 00:06:01,145
in the agent's workspace.

172
00:06:01,145 --> 00:06:01,501
Then,

173
00:06:01,501 --> 00:06:02,925
archiving artifacts,

174
00:06:02,925 --> 00:06:03,210
and,

175
00:06:03,210 --> 00:06:04,420
stashed one file.

176
00:06:04,970 --> 00:06:06,919
Stage two: running on Jenkins,

177
00:06:06,919 --> 00:06:08,868
in the controller's workspace.

178
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:10,298
And there is the file,

179
00:06:10,298 --> 00:06:11,532
cloud cart dot war,

180
00:06:11,532 --> 00:06:13,546
arrived from the other machine.

181
00:06:14,096 --> 00:06:15,354
Now the build page.

182
00:06:15,354 --> 00:06:16,413
Under the build,

183
00:06:16,413 --> 00:06:17,605
the archived file,

184
00:06:17,605 --> 00:06:18,863
cloud cart dot war,

185
00:06:18,863 --> 00:06:20,055
ready to download.

186
00:06:20,055 --> 00:06:21,644
It stays with the build,

187
00:06:21,644 --> 00:06:23,696
even if the workspace is wiped.

188
00:06:24,246 --> 00:06:28,933
The workspaces link lists the folder on each machine that ran this build.

189
00:06:28,933 --> 00:06:30,024
One on the agent,

190
00:06:30,024 --> 00:06:31,436
one on the controller.

191
00:06:31,436 --> 00:06:33,106
I open the controller one,

192
00:06:33,106 --> 00:06:35,160
and the unstashed file is here,

193
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,921
only because the second stage asked for it.

194
00:06:38,471 --> 00:06:39,421
One more thing,

195
00:06:39,421 --> 00:06:41,448
the mistake everyone makes once.

196
00:06:41,448 --> 00:06:43,032
We create a new Pipeline,

197
00:06:43,032 --> 00:06:44,680
and name it needs windows.

198
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:45,820
In the script box,

199
00:06:45,820 --> 00:06:49,811
we type a script that asks for an agent with the label windows.

200
00:06:49,811 --> 00:06:50,382
Remember,

201
00:06:50,382 --> 00:06:52,156
no machine wears that label.

202
00:06:52,156 --> 00:06:53,169
Then we save it.

203
00:07:07,719 --> 00:07:08,372
Build Now.

204
00:07:08,372 --> 00:07:09,938
The build does not fail.

205
00:07:09,938 --> 00:07:10,525
It waits.

206
00:07:10,525 --> 00:07:11,634
Open the console.

207
00:07:11,634 --> 00:07:13,657
Still waiting to schedule task.

208
00:07:13,657 --> 00:07:16,397
There are no nodes with the label windows.

209
00:07:16,397 --> 00:07:17,767
It will wait forever.

210
00:07:27,317 --> 00:07:28,533
When a build waits,

211
00:07:28,533 --> 00:07:29,685
read this message.

212
00:07:29,685 --> 00:07:30,453
It says why.

213
00:07:30,453 --> 00:07:31,861
Usually a wrong label,

214
00:07:31,861 --> 00:07:33,653
or an agent that is offline.

215
00:07:34,203 --> 00:07:35,863
That is the whole picture.

216
00:07:35,863 --> 00:07:37,394
A controller that plans,

217
00:07:37,394 --> 00:07:38,479
agents that work,

218
00:07:38,479 --> 00:07:39,692
labels that choose,

219
00:07:39,692 --> 00:07:41,670
and files that move on purpose.

220
00:07:43,220 --> 00:07:44,372
Five mistakes.

221
00:07:44,922 --> 00:07:47,379
One: running builds on the controller.

222
00:07:47,379 --> 00:07:49,837
Give it zero executors in a real team,

223
00:07:49,837 --> 00:07:51,130
and let agents work.

224
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:56,992
Two: one executor on a big machine. Match executors to the cores, and to the memory.

225
00:07:57,542 --> 00:08:02,513
Three: a label nobody wears. The build waits forever. Read the console message.

226
00:08:03,063 --> 00:08:07,009
Four: treating the workspace as storage. Archive what you need to keep.

227
00:08:07,559 --> 00:08:09,592
Five: archiving huge folders.

228
00:08:09,592 --> 00:08:12,045
Archive only the files people need,

229
00:08:12,045 --> 00:08:14,919
and stash only what the next stage needs.

230
00:08:16,469 --> 00:08:19,264
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

231
00:08:19,814 --> 00:08:21,278
One: the repository,

232
00:08:21,278 --> 00:08:25,598
GitHub dot com slash it dash waves slash devops-ai,

233
00:08:25,598 --> 00:08:27,942
in the folder academy slash lab.

234
00:08:28,492 --> 00:08:34,124
Two: the files, lab one sixty dot S H, and shortcuts one sixty dot S H.

235
00:08:34,674 --> 00:08:40,135
Three: install it, with sudo install, into slash user slash local slash S bin.

236
00:08:40,685 --> 00:08:42,524
Four: load the short names,

237
00:08:42,524 --> 00:08:45,250
with source shortcuts one sixty dot S H.

238
00:08:45,250 --> 00:08:46,067
Then lab up,

239
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:47,021
and lab agent.

240
00:08:47,571 --> 00:08:50,067
Five: lab agent creates the agent user,

241
00:08:50,067 --> 00:08:52,691
and prints the one command to connect it.

242
00:08:52,691 --> 00:08:55,507
Lab files writes the three pipeline scripts.

243
00:08:56,057 --> 00:08:59,689
Six: you need the Jenkins from lesson one fifty-five,

244
00:08:59,689 --> 00:09:00,306
and Java.

245
00:09:00,306 --> 00:09:03,801
Lab down stops the agent and removes the lab files.

246
00:09:04,351 --> 00:09:05,994
The link is in the description.

247
00:09:08,044 --> 00:09:09,815
Your turn, on your own machine.

248
00:09:10,365 --> 00:09:13,735
One: lab up, then lab agent, and read the command it prints.

249
00:09:14,285 --> 00:09:17,485
Two: add the node in the Jenkins screens, and connect it.

250
00:09:18,035 --> 00:09:21,555
Three: run the agent test, three times, and watch the queue.

251
00:09:22,105 --> 00:09:26,159
Four: run the cloud cart pipeline, and download the archived file.

252
00:09:26,709 --> 00:09:31,957
Five: ask for a label nobody wears, and read the console message. Then lab down.

253
00:09:32,507 --> 00:09:34,341
Pause the video, and begin now.

254
00:09:49,891 --> 00:09:50,766
Quick check.

255
00:09:51,316 --> 00:09:54,132
What is the difference between a controller and an agent?

256
00:09:54,682 --> 00:09:55,983
What is an executor?

257
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:58,816
When do you archive, and when do you stash?

258
00:09:59,366 --> 00:10:01,030
Why does a build wait forever?

259
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:04,070
Objective covered: M C seventeen,

260
00:10:04,070 --> 00:10:05,278
objective seven.

261
00:10:05,278 --> 00:10:06,712
Distributed agents,

262
00:10:06,712 --> 00:10:08,598
workspaces and artifacts.

263
00:10:09,148 --> 00:10:11,218
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

264
00:10:21,768 --> 00:10:25,437
Next: approval, promotion, rollback and notifications.

265
00:10:25,987 --> 00:10:29,315
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
